    _a .more href="https://yr-lang.org/docs"
      Full reference
  _section #try .block
    _h2
      Try yr
    _p
      This is a real Yr file running in your browser. Edit it and the preview updates.
    _ .yrkit-preview
      _ .yrkit-preview__bar
        _span .yrkit-preview__filename
          preview.yr
      _ .yrkit-preview__editor-wrap
        _ #yr-gutter .yrkit-preview__gutter aria-hidden="true"
        _ .yrkit-preview__scroll
          _pre #yr-mirror .yrkit-preview__mirror aria-hidden="true"
          _textarea #yr-editor .yrkit-preview__editor spellcheck="false" wrap="off" autocapitalize="off" autocomplete="off" autocorrect="off" aria-label="Editor de código yr"
      _iframe #yr-preview-frame .yrkit-preview__frame sandbox="allow-scripts allow-modals allow-forms" title="Pré-visualização"
  _section #build .hero
    _
      _p .crumb
        AI
      _h2
        A language easy for AI to build with.
      _p .lead
        yr keeps a whole web project in one file, split by simple markers. The AI reads everything at once, changes only the section you asked for, and you can still read every line.
      _ .actions
        _a .btn href="https://app.yrkit.com/"
          Try it in Yrkit
        _a .btn.ghost href="https://yr-lang.org/docs"
          Read the docs
      _p .status
        Open source, v0.x, early stage. yr has no variables or loops of its own: logic lives in the JavaScript sections. What is here works, and it runs Yrkit in production.
    _ .panel
      _p .ask
        Turn the title red and add a /health route.
      _ .file
        _ .tab
        _ .code role="img" aria-label="A yr file with sections for body, CSS, frontend JavaScript and backend JavaScript. The frontend and backend lines added by the AI are highlighted."
      _p .cap
        Only the
        _code
          @@
        and
        _code
          &amp;&amp;
        sections changed. The rest stayed as it was.
  _section #why .block
    _h2
      Why AI writes yr well
    _p
      Most projects are spread over dozens of files. yr is built the other way around.
    _ .cols
      _
        _h3
          The whole feature in one place
        _p
          Page, style, browser code, server code and deploy scripts sit in the same
          _code
            &#46;yr
          file. The AI reads a complete feature at once instead of chasing imports across folders.
      _
        _h3
          Sections are clear boundaries
        _p
          Every section starts with a two-character marker. The AI finds the part to change, edits it, and leaves the rest of the file alone.
      _
        _h3
          Nothing new inside
        _p
          Inside each section it is plain HTML, CSS, JavaScript, Node or Bash, which every AI already knows. The only new thing is a short list of markers.
  _section #teach .block
    _h2
      Teach any AI yr in one paste
    _p
      Copy this cheat sheet into your AI assistant, then ask it for a
      _code
        &#46;yr
      file. It covers the markers you need for a full page.
    _ .spec-head
      _span
        llm.txt
      _button #copy .btn.ghost type="button"
        Copy
    _pre #spec tabindex="0"
      Loading…
  _section #api .block
    _article #api-doc .readme aria-busy="true"
      _p .readme__status
        Loading documentation…
  _section #syntax .block
    _article #syntax-doc .readme aria-busy="true"
      _p .readme__status
        Loading documentation…
  _section #examples .block
    _article #examples-doc .readme aria-busy="true"
      _p .readme__status
        Loading documentation…
  _section #yrkit .block
    _h2
      Yrkit is written in yr
    _p
      Yrkit is the app where you build systems by talking to an AI. You describe what you want in plain language, and it writes the whole project for you.
    _p
      It is written entirely in yr. Building Yrkit is what pushed the language forward: wherever the project needed something the language could not do yet, the language grew. Today it is the largest project running on yr, and it works in production.
    _ .shots
      _figure
        _img src="https://yrkit.site/yrkit-gif5.gif" alt="A chat prompt in Yrkit on the left and the generated app running on the right" loading="lazy"
        _figcaption
          A prompt in, a working app out.
      _figure
        _img src="https://yrkit.site/yrkit-gif6.gif" alt="The single .yr file behind the generated project, with its sections and markers visible" loading="lazy"
        _figcaption
          The whole project stays in one .yr file you can read and edit.
    _ .actions
      _a .btn href="https://yrkit.com/"
        See Yrkit
  _section #yr-cli .block
    _h2
      yr-cli
    _p
      yr-cli is the command line tool for yr. It builds, serves and deploys your projects from the terminal.
    _p
      Install it globally with npm:
    _pre .snippet
      npm install -g @yr-lang/yr-cli
    _ .actions
      _a .btn href="https://www.npmjs.com/package/@yr-lang/yr-cli"
        View on npm
      _a .btn.ghost href="https://github.com/yr-lang/yr"
        GitHub
  _section #free .block
    _h2
      Free to use, free to study
    _ .cols
      _
        _h3
          yr
        _p
          The language itself: parser, compiler and runtime. MIT-compatible for personal and commercial use.
        _a href="https://github.com/yr-lang/yr"
          GitHub
      _
        _h3
          yr-cli
        _p
          Command line tools: build, serve and deploy. Install globally with npm and run Yr projects anywhere.
        _a href="https://www.npmjs.com/package/@yr-lang/yr-cli"
          npm
      _
        _h3
          @yr-lang/yr
        _p
          The npm package. Use Yr from your own Node.js projects or inside your own tools.
        _a href="https://www.npmjs.com/package/@yr-lang/yr"
          npm
  _section #support .block
    _h2
      Support the project
    _p
      yr is a solo developer project. If it is useful to you, consider supporting its development. It helps keep the infrastructure running and the language moving forward.
    _ .actions
      _a .btn href="https://github.com/sponsors/mwtheus"
